  },
  {
    "episode_id": 64496,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64496.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Well, I was obviously a very powerful speech, a powerful moment. It's easier to have power behind you when history and when the facts are on your side. And I just think that's the case here. I mean, the Prime Minister has very obvious concerns and there's no question that I think he was persuasive and present goes today.",
