    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 64496,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64496.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I read your article in the Wall Street Journal, in what way is Iran a reliable negotiating partner question mark and boy. That question mark looms large and I thought it was interesting when the Prime Minister said This is a very bad deal. We're better off without it. And then he went on to say, this bad deal won't, if we reject this bad deal, it won't lead to war, it will lead to a better deal. And basically challenged us and the rest of the world to call Iran's bluff.",
