    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 64496,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64496.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. And you know, the administration sets up this straw man that the option is, well, you've either got to sign this deal or go to war, and that's not true at all. I mean, there's a third option. It's very obvious the Prime Minister said it and that is to negotiate a better deal. And that's what all of us are hoping and encouraging the president to do. But this deal, as is presently negotiated, it does not preclude Iran from receiving nuclear weapons or developing nuclear weapons. It, in fact, almost guarantees that they will develop nuclear weapons. All it does is it precludes them over the next few years. I mean, you say, well, 10 years down the road. And I asked, do you think that they will be any better, any more friendly to the West 10 years down the road? Do you think they will have given up their regional ambitions 10 years down the road? Will they be more powerful or less powerful? And they're going to be more powerful because we will have lifted the sanctions. And I just can't understand what the administration is thinking. Why do they think it's acceptable to delay this for 10 years, but then nearly guarantee at that point that they will nuclearize their programs?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The current deal does not prevent Iran from eventually acquiring nuclear weapons.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The administration presents a false dichotomy between signing the deal and going to war.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The current deal effectively guarantees that Iran will develop nuclear weapons after the initial restrictions expire.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "There exists a viable third option: negotiating a better deal.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Lifting sanctions under the deal will enhance Iran’s capabilities and strength.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Iran’s power and regional ambitions are expected to increase over the next ten years.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the administration’s strategy is irrational or poorly thought out.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker expects Iran will not become more friendly toward the West in ten years.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "A long-term commitment to non-proliferation requires preventing future nuclear development, not merely delaying it.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
