    "turn_text": "Yeah, it really was, and you know, Look, there's no question that the vice president and secretary of state made the decision to leave the country. They made announced their travel plans after we knew that the prime minister was going to come visit with us. And there's no question they did that to send a message. And, you know, it's interesting too, we're meeting with groups, you know, that generally, you know, the Jewish community is generally supportive of Democrats and liberal causes that it really puts them in a bind. And frankly, it puts the Democrats in the bind. I had a what they call a special order last night on the house floor. Well, for one hour, we invited members to come down and to speak on this topic. And I invited many Democrats to come down and join me and not one of them would. And I'm shocked at that. I mean, I'm seriously stunned at that. This is something that shouldn't be partisan and wouldn't have been partisan before. But, you know, gosh, I think the clarity of this is really clear. I mean, do you stand for is or do you not?",
